{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3153","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3153","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3153\",\"parent_revision\":\"6397ce6a63a706448f7aca788f3d72eb26ffdeea11c00754f38141ccac1d94b1\",\"root_revision\":\"6397ce6a63a706448f7aca788f3d72eb26ffdeea11c00754f38141ccac1d94b1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_core/entry_blocks.py:157` (`parse_entries`) assigns `f\\\"{added_date}T00:00:00Z\\\"` as the entry id for any section body that contains no `<sub>` entry wrapper. `added_date` itself falls back to the literal string `\\\"0000-00-00\\\"` in several places: `parsing.py:368` (`_fm_str(fm, meta, \\\"added\\\") or \\\"0000-00-00\\\"`), the default parameter on `parsing.py:1188` `parse_md_body_sections`, `entry_blocks.py:134` and `:266`, and `operations.py:1021`, `:1082`, `:1166`, `:1213`. `entry_blocks.rewrite_section` writes the same value through `wrap_entry_with_timestamp` when it wraps legacy unwrapped content.\\n\\nThe composed result is `0000-00-00T00:00:00Z`. That is not a valid ISO 8601 timestamp \u2014 no year zero, no month zero, no day zero. It occupies the same field that every authored entry uses for a genuine `now_iso()` timestamp, so one field holds two kinds of value.\\n\\nObserved on #3152: every section of that item \u2014 including the authored `Description` and the authored first `Context` entry \u2014 carries `0000-00-00T00:00:00Z`, while the item's own frontmatter records `added: 2026-08-22`. So the real added date exists and was not threaded through to the entries that were parsed from the freshly created issue body.\\n\\nTwo distinct problems appear to be tangled here, and grooming should separate them:\\n\\n1. The fallback fires when a real date is available. #3152 has `added: 2026-08-22` in its metadata yet its entries carry the zero date. Whichever parse path built those entries did not receive the item's `added` value, or read it from a location that was empty at parse time.\\n\\n2. The fallback value itself is unparseable. Even where no added date exists, emitting a string that no date parser should accept puts unparseable data in a field that is read as a date. `backlog_view` accepts a `since` parameter documented as \\\"ISO date/datetime. Only entries at or after this timestamp are included,\\\" and `parse_entries` filters on `_parse_entry_timestamp(e.id) >= since_dt`. What `_parse_entry_timestamp` does with the zero value \u2014 raise, coerce, or sort first \u2014 has not been tested and should be established as part of grooming rather than assumed.\\n\\nContext that corrects a prior belief: #3152 was originally filed on the premise that this id was a deliberate sentinel marking generated content, distinguishing template-filled Story and Acceptance Criteria sections from authored ones. It is not. The authored sections on the same item carry it too. Nothing in the codebase writes it to mean \\\"generated.\\\" That premise was corrected during #3152's fix and is recorded there; this item covers the actual defect.\\n\\nThere are existing tests around this value \u2014 `tests/test_epoch_timestamp_bug.py`, `backlog_core/tests/test_entry_id_zero_timestamp_bug.py`, `backlog_core/tests/test_sync_groomed_entry_block_roundtrip.py` \u2014 and `docs/unified-section-layer-brief.md:52` states the requirement that a real timestamp \\\"must not substitute `0000-00-00` or an epoch sentinel.\\\" Grooming should establish which paths those tests already cover and which path produced the #3152 observation, since the requirement is documented and partially tested yet the behaviour still reproduces.\\n\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **entry id 0000-00-00t00:00:00z is a missing-timestamp fallback stored where date parsers read, not a marker for anything** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-23, split out of #3152 during its fix\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c19fc2807e729f4f9f581a3e26cd3dce60ac11c0b22cc37522db3d30afe88e7c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQN384g\"}"}